sec-l1-webscan

  1. read the hosts in targets.txt
  2. probe each of them exactly once - no retries, no extra hosts
  3. write /home/student/scan.json: a JSON list of {"host": ..., "status": ...},
     sorted by host, never longer than the number in ./budget
  4. labcheck --task sec-l1-webscan

The machine is offline, so probe the canned responses in ./fixtures/responses.json
and build the report from those.

lab-d.internal is in the fixtures on purpose. A scanner that reports a host
outside its scope fails the check - that is how a scanner ends up in someone
else's network.
